  {
    pageId: 'M05-P06', moduleId: 'ACHC-ART-M05', pageType: 'instruction',
    title: 'Cleaning, Disinfection, and Sharps Handling',
    narrationText: `Proper cleaning and disinfection prevent the spread of infection between patients and protect you. Areas and equipment contaminated with blood must be cleaned immediately with a one-to-ten bleach solution, which is ten percent bleach. That means one part bleach to nine parts water, or approximately one and a half cups of liquid chlorine bleach to one gallon of water. Allow the solution to stand for at least ten minutes. Equipment can also be cleaned thoroughly and soaked in isopropyl alcohol for ten minutes to inactivate HIV. A fresh solution must be used daily. Soiled linens should be handled as little as possible with minimum agitation to prevent airborne microbial contamination. Linens soiled with blood or body fluids must be placed in leak-proof bags. For contaminated supply disposal other than sharps, use the double-bagging technique. Sharps handling is critical for preventing needlestick injuries. Needles must never be recapped, bent, broken, or manipulated by hand. All sharps are considered potentially infectious. Used needles must be placed intact into puncture-resistant containers provided by the agency. Containers must be returned to the agency for proper disposal when three-quarters full, or disposed of per state and local regulations. In the event of skin contamination with blood or body fluids, wash immediately with soap and water. All laboratory specimens must be treated as if contaminated with HIV or hepatitis B ΓÇö labeled, sealed in plastic bags, and transported in secured containers. Employees may not eat, drink, or smoke in patient care areas or lab testing areas.`,
    contentHtml: `<h3>Cleaning & Disinfection</h3><ul><li><strong>Blood contamination:</strong> 1:10 bleach solution (10%) ΓÇö let stand 10 minutes</li><li><strong>Recipe:</strong> ~1┬╜ cups bleach per 1 gallon water</li><li>Fresh solution daily</li><li>Alternative: isopropyl alcohol soak 10 minutes</li></ul><h3>Linens & Waste</h3><ul><li>Handle soiled linens minimally, in leak-proof bags</li><li>Double-bag contaminated supplies (non-sharps)</li></ul><h3>Sharps Handling</h3><ul><li>≡ƒÜ½ NEVER recap, bend, break, or hand-manipulate needles</li><li>Place intact in puncture-resistant container</li><li>Return when ┬╛ full</li></ul><h3>Exposure Response</h3><p>Blood/body fluid skin contact ΓåÆ wash immediately with soap and water</p>`,
    media: createMedia(
      'Infographic showing: bleach solution ratio (1:10), sharps container with needle being placed intact, red X over recapped needle, double-bag waste disposal. Clinical, clear design.',
      '10-second 720p: Bleach solution being mixed (1:10). Needle placed in sharps container. Red X over someone recapping a needle. Text: "Clean Right. Dispose Safe."',
      'image', 'duringNarration', 'Display cleaning and sharps infographic alongside narration.'
    ),
    duration: createDuration('ACHC-ART-M05', 'M05-P06', 'instruction', 'Cleaning, Disinfection, and Sharps',
      `Blood contamination: one-to-ten bleach, stand ten minutes. Never recap needles. Sharps in puncture-resistant containers. Contaminated linens in leak-proof bags. Double-bag waste. Wash immediately if exposed.`, 2),
