  {
    pageId: 'M05-P07', moduleId: 'ACHC-ART-M05', pageType: 'instruction',
    title: 'Exposure Response and Reportable Diseases',
    narrationText: `If you are exposed to blood or potentially infectious material, take immediate action. For needlestick injuries, cuts, or exposed skin, wash thoroughly with soap and water. If splashed around the mouth or nose, flush with water. If splashed in or around the eyes, irrigate with clean water, saline, or sterile irrigant for twenty minutes. Report the incident immediately to the appropriate person in your agency's exposure control plan and to emergency medical services if they take over care. Record the incident with the date, time, circumstances, actions taken, and any information required by your employer. Seek immediate follow-up care as identified in the exposure control plan. Your agency is also responsible for reporting certain infectious diseases to the public health department. When a staff member becomes aware of a reportable infection in a patient, they must inform the Director of Nursing or Director of Quality Improvement. After confirming the infection through record review and physician discussion, a reporting form is completed and forwarded to the health department. A copy goes to the patient's physician. The agency maintains a log of all reported infections. Examples of reportable conditions include communicable diseases, TB, and other conditions as defined by your state health department. The agency obtains the current reportable disease list from the state department of health.`,
    contentHtml: `<h3>Exposure Response ΓÇö Immediate Actions</h3><ol><li><strong>Needlestick/cut/skin:</strong> Wash with soap and water</li><li><strong>Mouth/nose splash:</strong> Flush with water</li><li><strong>Eye splash:</strong> Irrigate 20 minutes with clean water/saline</li><li><strong>Report immediately</strong> to supervisor per exposure control plan</li><li><strong>Document:</strong> date, time, circumstances, actions</li><li><strong>Follow-up care</strong> per exposure control plan</li></ol><h3>Reportable Diseases</h3><ul><li>Staff notifies DON or QI Director when aware of reportable infection</li><li>Confirmed ΓåÆ report to local health department</li><li>Copy to patient's physician</li><li>Log maintained of all reported infections</li></ul>`,
