    title: 'Patient and Caregiver Infection Prevention Teaching',
    narrationText: `Teaching patients and caregivers about infection prevention is a core responsibility. Materials must be appropriate to the patient's educational level, literacy, and language. Key teaching topics include proper hand hygiene technique and when to wash, signs and symptoms of infection such as redness, warmth, swelling, drainage, odor, and fever, how to handle soiled linens and dispose of contaminated materials, the importance of not sharing personal care items, when to notify the agency about changes in condition, respiratory hygiene including covering coughs and sneezes, and proper medication use particularly antibiotics taken as prescribed. Use the teach-back method to verify understanding. Ask the patient or caregiver to demonstrate hand washing or to describe infection signs in their own words. Document what you taught, how you taught it, and whether the learner demonstrated understanding.`,
