    narrationText: `Review key concepts: Standard precautions apply to every patient based on exposure, not diagnosis. Hand hygiene is number one. Alcohol sanitizer is preferred except for C-diff which requires soap and water. Minimum soap wash time is fifteen seconds. PPE selection is based on anticipated exposure: gloves for fluids, goggles for splash, gowns for spray, masks for respiratory. Bag technique: never on the floor, barrier required, double-bag for vermin or virulent organisms. Blood cleanup: one-to-ten bleach, stand ten minutes. Sharps: never recap, puncture-resistant containers, return at three-quarters full. Eye exposure: irrigate twenty minutes. Report immediately. Equipment cleaned before returning to bag. Weekly bag exterior wipe. Monthly full cleanout. Retake after review.`,
