    // M09 Pages 6-10: Scenario, documentation, additional instruction
    { pageId: 'M09-P06', moduleId: 'ACHC-ART-M09', pageType: 'scenario-challenge', title: 'Compliance Scenario: Field Situation',
      narrationText: `You discover that a colleague has been clocking in for patient visits at homes she never actually visited. She tells you she was "making up visits" because her caseload numbers were low and she feared losing her position. She asks you not to say anything. This is a clear case of fraud ΓÇö billing for services not rendered. Your compliance obligations require you to report this regardless of your personal relationship with the colleague. Consider the consequences: false claims to Medicare or Medicaid, patient records showing visits that did not occur affecting care decisions, potential harm to the agency including fines, sanctions, and loss of certification. Report to the CCO immediately.`,
      contentHtml: `<h3>Fraud Scenario</h3><p>Colleague fabricating patient visits and asking you to stay silent.</p>`,
